rification of colored water of low turbidity, containing anthropogenic admixtures.<br />The model illustrates the possibilities for simplifying the optimization problems, when the decisions are taken in advance about exclusion the optimization parameters of the functioning of constructions for treatment and repetitive utilization of the washing water and sludge treatment in the process of exploitation of the water purification stations.<br />This exclusion is permissible in the cases, when the possibilities are strictly limited or impossible at all in the given particular conditions for realization of a few modes of exploitation of the constructions of the washing water purification and also sludge treatment.<br />That is possible, for example, when the washing water is discharged for dilution into the water current downstream from the site of water intake and location of water purification station.<br />This can be performed on the economical reasons, when the exploitation expenditures for these blocks affect insignificantly on the general tendency of the changing reduced expenditures for the entire station.<br />Figure 2.<br />Structure model of optimization of the technological process of purification of the colored water with low turbidity<br />When the mathematical models of the complex of technological processes are formulated, it is supposed that the water purification station consists of a few constructions (modules) through which the initial water passes in series.<br />Each module affects water quality.<br />The outlet characteristics of quality of water coming out from one module are the initial characteristics for the following one.<br />Let the particular characteristics of the water quality, (for example turbidity, color index, oxidizing capability) will be designated as HTM1 or HTM2 , where HTM3 is a vector of the water quality characteristics and n is a number of the quality characteristics taking into account.<br />Every module affects one or few qu